.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-CREATE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-create - Create a durable tunnel


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel create <name> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a durable tunnel that serves a service on this machine. The machine must be enrolled
first (pb pair). Give the tunnel a name of 1 to 63 letters, digits, ".", "_" or "-",
not starting with punctuation, and its origin with --port (a local TCP port) or --from (an
origin URL: http, https, h2c, tcp or unix).

.PP
Access defaults to public. --private requires authenticated private access and --team requires an explicit team grant; they cannot be combined. --domain adds
a custom hostname after creation. By default the tunnel never expires; --duration sets a
lifetime, and pb tunnel extend moves it later.

.PP
A change returns once the request is accepted, and the tunnel may still be connecting. Pass
--wait to wait (at most --timeout, default 2m, 1s to 10m) until it finishes, or check pb tunnel
status.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--domain\fP=[]
	custom domain to add after creation (repeatable)

.PP
\fB--duration\fP=0s
	tunnel lifetime (default: the tunnel does not expire)

.PP
\fB--from\fP=""
	origin URL: http, https, h2c, tcp or unix (instead of --port)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--port\fP=0
	local TCP port to serve (or use --from)

.PP
\fB--private\fP[=false]
	require authenticated private access

.PP
\fB--team\fP[=false]
	require an explicit team grant for browser access

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=2m0s
	maximum time to wait for operation completion

.PP
\fB--wait\fP[=false]
	wait for the operation to reach a terminal state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb tunnel create web --port 8080
  pb tunnel create api --from http://127.0.0.1:9000 --private
  pb tunnel create docs --port 3000 --domain docs.example.com --wait
  pb tunnel create temp --port 8080 --duration 24h
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel(1)\fP
